1
00:00:04,913 --> 00:00:07,721
The Life of Muhammadﷺ,

2
00:00:07,857 --> 00:00:12,566
The Madinan period, volume 1, by Imam Anwar Al-Awlaki

3
00:00:13,117 --> 00:00:16,294
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝

4
00:00:16,803 --> 00:00:19,468
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

5
00:00:19,824 --> 00:00:25,058
الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ۝

6
00:00:25,328 --> 00:00:29,195
الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ۝

7
00:00:29,509 --> 00:00:33,064
مَالِكِ يَوْمِ الدِّينِ۝

8
00:00:33,253 --> 00:00:37,667
إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِين۝

9
00:00:38,414 --> 00:00:42,554
اهْدِنَا الصِّرَاطَ الْمُسْتَقِيمَ۝

10
00:00:42,664 --> 00:00:54,812
صِرَاطَ الَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ غَيْرِ الْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا الضَّالِّينَ۝

11
00:00:56,108 --> 00:00:59,116
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝ بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

12
00:00:59,466 --> 00:01:05,286
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْراَ

13
00:01:05,656 --> 00:01:08,117
السلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

14
00:01:09,571 --> 00:01:14,804
In sha Allah Ta'ala(اِنْ شَاءالله تعالى), we'll start with the Hijrah(هجرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

15
00:01:16,634 --> 00:01:21,243
I've already covered in the past the life of Rasool Allah ﷺ in Makkah

16
00:01:21,980 --> 00:01:28,066
So, In sha Allah Ta'ala(اِنْ شَاءالله تعالى) in these sessions, we'll talk about the early stage of Madina

17
00:01:28,785 --> 00:01:30,441
and we'll start with Al-Hijrah(الهجرة).

18
00:01:31,309 --> 00:01:34,325
But before that just the word on Seerah(سيرة).

19
00:01:35,206 --> 00:01:40,605
The books of Seerah(سيرة) are concerned with what usually historians are concerned with,

20
00:01:40,669 --> 00:01:47,120
 and that's the history of politics and the history of the military engagements.

21
00:01:49,002 --> 00:01:53,230
When it comes to the Akhlaaq(أخلاق) of Rasool Allahﷺ, you'd find those in the books of Hadith(حديث).

22
00:01:54,058 --> 00:01:57,043
If you're interested in the Shamael(شمائل) of Rasool Ullah,

23
00:01:57,217 --> 00:02:02,598
which are issues relating to his character, you would find those in books of Shamael(شمائل).

24
00:02:03,019 --> 00:02:12,497
However, the books of Seerah(سيرة) usually cover the political and military aspects of the life of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

25
00:02:13,368 --> 00:02:16,704
And that's why many of our scholars called Seerah(سيرة), Maghazi(مغازي),

26
00:02:16,974 --> 00:02:18,886
Maghazi(مغازي) means, battles.

27
00:02:21,563 --> 00:02:25,325
However, will try to bring in, the verses of Qur'an

28
00:02:25,603 --> 00:02:30,667
that relate to the events that were happening in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ

29
00:02:30,707 --> 00:02:36,088
 because Qur'an would comment on events that happened in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

30
00:02:36,692 --> 00:02:39,986
sometimes the Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an would proceed an event,

31
00:02:40,218 --> 00:02:43,528
sometimes Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an would come concurrent with an event

32
00:02:43,568 --> 00:02:47,478
and sometimes the Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an would come to comment on an event.

33
00:02:47,819 --> 00:02:52,208
So, for example, you have Ghazwa-Tul-Anfaal(غزوة الأنفال) was revealed, talking about the Battle of Badr(بدر),

34
00:02:52,303 --> 00:02:53,597
and what happened therein.

35
00:02:54,874 --> 00:03:01,961
The Battle of Uhud(أحَد), you have the end of the Surah(سورة) of Al-Imran(العمران), relates the story of Uhud(أحَد),

36
00:03:02,822 --> 00:03:06,223
Surah-Tul-Hashr(سورة الحشر) talks about the Battle of Bannu Nadhir(بنو نضير).

37
00:03:07,181 --> 00:03:12,328
You have the Surah(سورة) of Al-Munafiqoon(المنافقون) and Surah-Tun-Noor(سورة النور), the Battle of Bann Mustalaq(بنو مصطلق).

38
00:03:12,993 --> 00:03:17,775
And you have Surah-Tul-Ahzaab(سورة الاحزاب) relating what happened in the Battle of the trench.

39
00:03:19,389 --> 00:03:24,139
So, we'll try to bring in these verses that relate to these events in Seerah(سيرة).

40
00:03:25,173 --> 00:03:27,860
We'll start with the Hijrah(هجرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

41
00:03:27,900 --> 00:03:31,927
Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed Ayaat(آيات) in Makkah, talking about Al-Hijrah(ألهجرة).

42
00:03:32,403 --> 00:03:33,744
 Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

43
00:03:34,141 --> 00:03:39,196
قُلْ يَا عِبَادِ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اتَّقُوا رَبَّكُمْ ۚ

44
00:03:39,371 --> 00:03:44,356
لِلَّذِينَ أَحْسَنُوا فِي هَٰذِهِ الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةٌ ۗ

45
00:03:44,595 --> 00:03:47,245
وَأَرْضُ اللَّهِ وَاسِعَةٌ ۗ

46
00:03:47,507 --> 00:03:55,621
إِنَّمَا يُوَفَّى الصَّابِرُونَ أَجْرَهُمْ بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ۝

47
00:03:56,197 --> 00:03:58,814
Say O my servants who have believed,

48
00:03:59,587 --> 00:04:04,462
Fear your Lord, for those who do good in this world, is good.

49
00:04:04,897 --> 00:04:07,056
And the earth of Allah is spacious,

50
00:04:07,357 --> 00:04:10,675
 indeed the patient will be given their reward without account.

51
00:04:11,149 --> 00:04:12,524
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ in this Ayah(آية) says;

52
00:04:12,564 --> 00:04:14,012
 وَأَرْضُ اللَّهِ وَاسِعَةٌ ۗ

53
00:04:14,462 --> 00:04:18,990
The earth of Allah is spacious meaning that if you are suffering oppression in Makkah,

54
00:04:19,204 --> 00:04:21,642
then you can move somewhere else,

55
00:04:21,824 --> 00:04:26,658
where you will be able to apply and live the religion of Allahعَزّوجَل.

56
00:04:27,657 --> 00:04:31,687
Mujahid(مجاهد), who's one of Al-Mufassiroon(ألمفسرون), one of the Imams of Tafseer(تفسير).

57
00:04:32,032 --> 00:04:33,947
He says; Commenting about this Ayah(آية)

58
00:04:34,102 --> 00:04:36,923
فَهَاجَرُوْ فِيْهَا وَ جَاهِدُوْ وَعْتَزِلُ الْاَوْسَانْ

59
00:04:37,585 --> 00:04:40,235
He said: Make Hijrah(هجرة) in the land

60
00:04:40,829 --> 00:04:44,599
and fighting the path of Allahعَزّوجَلّ and stay away from the idol worshipping

61
00:04:45,228 --> 00:04:49,474
And Attaa(عطاء), one of the early scholars of this Ummah(امة), he says;

62
00:04:49,554 --> 00:04:52,217
اِذَ دُعِيْتُمْ اِلَى مَعْصِيَّتٍ فَحْرُبُوْ

63
00:04:52,603 --> 00:04:55,395
If you are invited to do a sin, then run away.

64
00:04:55,895 --> 00:04:57,705
So, we should run away from sins.

65
00:04:58,197 --> 00:05:02,300
And these two quotes are in the Tafseer(تفسير) of Ibn Kathir(إبن كثير).

66
00:05:03,142 --> 00:05:04,575
Allahعَزّوجَلّ also says;

67
00:05:05,220 --> 00:05:14,212
وَالَّذِينَ هَاجَرُوا فِي اللَّهِ مِنْ بَعْدِ مَا ظُلِمُوا لَنُبَوِّئَنَّهُمْ فِي الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً ۖ

68
00:05:14,966 --> 00:05:17,783
وَلَأَجْرُ الْآخِرَةِ أَكْبَرُ ۚ

69
00:05:17,982 --> 00:05:20,914
لَوْ كَانُوا يَعْلَمُونَ۝

70
00:05:21,188 --> 00:05:27,036
 الَّذِينَ صَبَرُوا وَعَلَىٰ رَبِّهِمْ يَتَوَكَّلُونَ۝

71
00:05:27,375 --> 00:05:32,134
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says; And those, who immigrated for Allah after they have been wronged,

72
00:05:32,415 --> 00:05:35,999
we will surely settle them in this world in a good place,

73
00:05:36,258 --> 00:05:39,957
but the reward of the Hereafter is greater if only they could know.

74
00:05:40,101 --> 00:05:41,102
So notice here,

75
00:05:41,392 --> 00:05:44,919
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is promising the ones, who make Hijrah(هجرة) for His sake,

76
00:05:45,322 --> 00:05:46,965
the ones who have been oppressed,

77
00:05:47,313 --> 00:05:51,978
Allah promises them that He will settle them in this world in a good place.

78
00:05:52,182 --> 00:05:53,388
 So, what does this mean?

79
00:05:54,111 --> 00:05:57,752
What does it mean, when Allahعَزّوجَلّ says we will settle them in this world in a good place?

80
00:05:58,423 --> 00:06:00,063
Some of the scholars of Tafseer(تفسير) said;

81
00:06:00,618 --> 00:06:01,962
if you look at Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون)

82
00:06:02,463 --> 00:06:05,651
the ones who moved of Makkah and went to Madina.

83
00:06:07,283 --> 00:06:12,257
Later on, every one of them became an Ameer(امير) of a state or a leader of an army.

84
00:06:12,963 --> 00:06:19,174
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ gave them a better status in this world than what they had in Makkah, that is in this world.

85
00:06:20,104 --> 00:06:25,006
And in Aakhira(آخرة) Allahعَزّوجَلّ says; But the reward of the Hereafter is greater.

86
00:06:25,793 --> 00:06:27,666
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) when he became Khalifah(خليفه)

87
00:06:27,706 --> 00:06:31,881
and he would give money or gifts to the Muhajiroon(مهاجرون),

88
00:06:31,921 --> 00:06:35,836
he would tell them, this is a gift from Allah for you in this world.

89
00:06:36,138 --> 00:06:39,200
 But what Allah has reserved for you in the Hereafter is even greater.

90
00:06:41,024 --> 00:06:45,038
And the scholars say, whoever leaves something for the sake of Allah,

91
00:06:45,244 --> 00:06:47,236
Allahعَزّوجَلّ will give him, something better.

92
00:06:48,438 --> 00:06:49,741
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

93
00:06:50,038 --> 00:06:59,381
ثُمَّ إِنَّ رَبَّكَ لِلَّذِينَ هَاجَرُوا مِنْ بَعْدِ مَا فُتِنُوا ثُمَّ جَاهَدُوا وَصَبَرُوا

94
00:07:00,024 --> 00:07:09,660
ثُمَّ جَاهَدُوا وَصَبَرُوا إِنَّ رَبَّكَ مِنْ بَعْدِهَا لَغَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ۝

95
00:07:10,087 --> 00:07:14,781
Then indeed, Your Lord to those who immigrated, after they had been compelled

96
00:07:15,142 --> 00:07:17,769
and thereafter fought and were patient.

97
00:07:18,079 --> 00:07:21,311
Indeed, your Lord after that, is Forgiving and Merciful.

98
00:07:21,766 --> 00:07:25,210
So, Hijrah(هجرة) has a very high status in Islam.

99
00:07:26,091 --> 00:07:30,493
These Muhajiroon(مهاجرون) have you ever asked yourself a question, Where did they stay?

100
00:07:30,774 --> 00:07:32,690
When they moved from Makkah to Madina?

101
00:07:33,261 --> 00:07:34,960
Did they check into hotels?

102
00:07:35,472 --> 00:07:37,415
Or did they stay in refugee camps?

103
00:07:38,274 --> 00:07:39,987
No, they stayed in the houses of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار).

104
00:07:40,995 --> 00:07:43,341
And that's why we call them Ansaar(أنصار),

105
00:07:44,407 --> 00:07:46,618
that's why we call them, the ones who gave victory to Islam.

106
00:07:46,643 --> 00:07:49,481
Ansaar(أنْصَار) means they gave support, they gave victory to the religion of Allah.

107
00:07:50,072 --> 00:07:52,516
Their houses were opened for Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون),

108
00:07:53,523 --> 00:07:56,824
even though they were very modest houses,

109
00:07:57,386 --> 00:07:59,283
for example Hassan Al-Basri(ألحسن ألبصري) says

110
00:07:59,323 --> 00:08:03,973
that I entered into the rooms of Rasool Allah ﷺ and I could touch the ceiling with my own hand.

111
00:08:04,337 --> 00:08:07,302
And when Rasool Allah ﷺ would pray in the room of Ayesha(عائشه).

112
00:08:07,986 --> 00:08:12,595
You know, every wife of Rasool Allah ﷺ had a room, that was it, just one room.

113
00:08:13,384 --> 00:08:19,939
You know, they didn't have like a kitchen and the living room and balcony and bedrooms, basement.

114
00:08:20,327 --> 00:08:22,760
No, every wife of Rasool Allah, just had one room.

115
00:08:23,204 --> 00:08:26,791
Now, when Rasool Allah ﷺ would pray in the room of Ayesha(عائشه).

116
00:08:27,815 --> 00:08:30,174
He would have to touch her

117
00:08:30,532 --> 00:08:35,322
so that she would move her feet away, so that he can make Sujood(سجود) it was that small.

118
00:08:36,166 --> 00:08:38,744
So for example, in the house of Khabeeb Ibn Isaaf(خبيب إبن إساف),

119
00:08:39,322 --> 00:08:43,049
Talha Bin Obaidillah(طلحه بن عبيدالله) his mother and Sohaib(صهيب), that's where, they stayed.

120
00:08:43,799 --> 00:08:45,924
Hamzah(حمزه) stayed in the house of Sa'ad Ibn Zurarah(اسعد بن زرارة).

121
00:08:46,713 --> 00:08:49,665
Sa'ad Bin Khaisamah(سعد بن خيسمه) all of the bachelors will stay in his house,

122
00:08:49,728 --> 00:08:51,363
so they called it, the house of bachelors.

123
00:08:51,955 --> 00:08:53,617
Ubaidah Bin Harissa(عبيدالله بن حارثه) and his mother

124
00:08:53,657 --> 00:08:57,054
At-Tufail Bin Haris(ألطفيل بن حارث), Tulail Bin Amr(طليل بن عمرو), Al-Hussain Bin Hariss(الحسين بن حارث),

125
00:08:57,658 --> 00:08:59,946
all of them stayed in the house of Abdullah Bin Salamah(عبدالله بن سلمه).

126
00:09:00,390 --> 00:09:06,004
So one thing we can learn is that being generous and being supportive of Muslims

127
00:09:06,535 --> 00:09:10,785
is one of the signs of Eeman(ايمان) and it was one of the signs of Al-Ansaarرضي الله عنهم.

128
00:09:12,706 --> 00:09:16,068
One comparison between the Hijrah(هجرة) to Madina and the Hijrah(هجرة) of Habasha(حبشه)

129
00:09:16,093 --> 00:09:17,675
because, you know, there are two Hijrah(هجرة),

130
00:09:18,206 --> 00:09:21,465
there was the first Hijrah(هجرة) to Al-Habasha(ألحبشه) and then there was the second Hijrah(هجرة) to Madina.

131
00:09:21,505 --> 00:09:22,863
 So, what's the difference between the two?

132
00:09:23,846 --> 00:09:26,886
Well, when it comes to the Hijrah(هجرة) to Al-Habasha(ألحبشه), it was more of,

133
00:09:28,730 --> 00:09:33,300
they went there to flee persecution, but they didn't become part of the society in Abyssinia,

134
00:09:33,989 --> 00:09:36,628
they weren't really part of the society, they were secluded.

135
00:09:37,410 --> 00:09:41,606
Therefore their ability to change the society was hindered.

136
00:09:43,581 --> 00:09:46,222
They were like refugees in Abyssinia.

137
00:09:47,197 --> 00:09:53,613
And that's why when they left Abyssinia, they didn't leave a strong Islamic impression behind.

138
00:09:54,425 --> 00:09:58,878
However, the Hijrah(هجرة) to Madina was an Hijrah(هجرة) to establish the Islamic community.

139
00:09:59,354 --> 00:10:00,924
 So, there is a big difference between the two.

140
00:10:02,573 --> 00:10:04,166
Some of the virtues of Madina,

141
00:10:04,768 --> 00:10:09,711
Rasool Allah ﷺ asked Allah to make them love Madina.

142
00:10:10,139 --> 00:10:10,825
So, he said;

143
00:10:10,944 --> 00:10:14,421
اَللَّهُمَّ حَبِّبْ إلينا الْمَدِيْنَهْ كَحُبِّنَا مَكَّة اَوْاَشَدّْ

144
00:10:15,030 --> 00:10:18,702
O Allah make us love Madina like we love Makkah or more.

145
00:10:19,967 --> 00:10:24,287
Rasool Allah ﷺ made Dua(دُعَا) that Allahعَزّوجَلّ gives Al-Madina Baraka(بركة),

146
00:10:24,725 --> 00:10:27,848
اَللَّهُمَّ الجْعَلْ بِالْمَدِيْنَهْ ضِعْفَيْ مَا جَعَلْتَ بِمَكَّةْ مِنَّ البَّرَكَة

147
00:10:27,872 --> 00:10:29,046
And this Hadith(حديث) is in Al-Bukhari(بخاريْ),

148
00:10:29,109 --> 00:10:37,231
O Allah, double the Baraka(بركة) double the blessings of Madina, compared to what you have given Makkah

149
00:10:37,334 --> 00:10:41,945
 because, who was the one who made Dua(دُعَا), to Allahعَزّوجَلّ to bless Makkah,

150
00:10:42,644 --> 00:10:43,912
it was Ibrahimعليه السّلام.

151
00:10:45,248 --> 00:10:51,466
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is asking Allahعَزّوجَلّ, to double that blessing, when it comes to Madina.

152
00:10:52,516 --> 00:10:54,161
Madina is protected from Ad-Dajjal(ألدجال),

153
00:10:54,796 --> 00:10:59,747
Rasool Allah ﷺ says that there are angels on every entrance to Madina protecting it, from Ad-Dajjal(ألدجال).

154
00:11:01,005 --> 00:11:05,652
There is a special reward for being patient on the hardship of Madina

155
00:11:05,715 --> 00:11:09,009
because Madina is, it was difficult to live in Madina at that time.

156
00:11:09,622 --> 00:11:13,392
It was very hot and the environment was harsh.

157
00:11:14,132 --> 00:11:15,156
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

158
00:11:15,211 --> 00:11:20,365
وَلَا يُثْبُتُ اَحَدْ عَلى لَأوَآءِهَا اِلَّا كُنْتُ شَفِيْعًا يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةْ

159
00:11:20,389 --> 00:11:22,598
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم),

160
00:11:22,859 --> 00:11:30,816
anyone who's patient on the hardships of Madina, I will be his intercessor on the Day of Judgment,

161
00:11:30,856 --> 00:11:34,190
I will intercede on his behalf on the Day of Judgment.

162
00:11:34,869 --> 00:11:37,698
There's a special blessing of dying in Madina.

163
00:11:38,126 --> 00:11:39,622
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

164
00:11:39,731 --> 00:11:44,265
مَنِ السْتَطَاعْ اَنْ يَمُوتَ بِالْمَدِيْنَةِ فَلْيَمُتْ بِهَا فَاِنِّيْ اَشْفَعُ لِمَنْ يَمُوْتُ فِيْهَا

165
00:11:44,598 --> 00:11:50,590
Whoever is able to die in Madina, then let it be so because I will intercede for you on the Day of Judgment.

166
00:11:51,028 --> 00:11:53,285
And this Hadith(حديث) is in Masnad Al-Imam Ahmad(مسند ألإمام أحمد).

167
00:11:53,676 --> 00:11:56,160
You know, Umar Ibn Al-Khattabرضي الله عنه, when he became Khalifah(خليفه).

168
00:11:56,879 --> 00:12:00,824
He wanted to die in Madina and he also wanted to die as a Shaheed(شهيد), he wanted to them both.

169
00:12:01,464 --> 00:12:06,486
So, he would make a Dua(دُعَا) to Allah, saying; O Allah, I want to die as a martyr in the town of your Prophet.

170
00:12:06,949 --> 00:12:08,318
So, his daughter Hafsah(حفصه) would tell him,

171
00:12:08,358 --> 00:12:12,723
O my father, How can you become a Shaheed(شهيد) in Madina, when it's safe?

172
00:12:13,175 --> 00:12:15,653
Madina is the capital of the Muslim Empire.

173
00:12:16,023 --> 00:12:20,285
If you want to die as a Shaheed(شهيد), you need to go to Iraq, you need to go to Syria, not in Madina.

174
00:12:21,501 --> 00:12:24,831
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) would say; "If Allah wants something to happen, He will make it happen."

175
00:12:25,558 --> 00:12:28,235
So not, only did Umar(عُمَر) die as Shaheed(شهيد) in Madina,

176
00:12:28,275 --> 00:12:31,996
he died as a Shaheed(شهيد) in the Mosque of Rasool Allah ﷺ and in Salah(صلاة).

177
00:12:33,880 --> 00:12:38,067
Madina is also the refuge of Eeman(إيمان), Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

178
00:12:38,092 --> 00:12:42,904
إن الإيمان ليأرز إلى المدينة كما تأرز الحية إلى جحرها

179
00:12:43,638 --> 00:12:45,474
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in Bukhari(بخاريْ) that

180
00:12:45,709 --> 00:12:51,381
Eeman(إيمان) seeks refuge in Madina or goes back to Madina like a snake would go back to its hole.

181
00:12:52,563 --> 00:12:58,091
Madina cleanses itself from the impure or the unclean.

182
00:12:58,464 --> 00:12:59,480
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

183
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:02,044
وَالَّذِيْ نَفْسِيْ بِيَدِهِ لَا يَخْرِجُ مِنْهَا اَحَدٌ

184
00:13:02,148 --> 00:13:05,291
رَغْبَةً عَنْهَا اِلَّا اَخْلَفَ اللهُ فِيْهَا خَيْرا مِّنْهُ،

185
00:13:05,584 --> 00:13:11,855
اَلَا اِنَّ الْمَدِيْنَةَ كَالْكِيْر، يخْرِجُ الْخَبِيْثَ ، لَا تَقُوْمُ السَّاعَةُ حَتَّي تَنْفِيَ الْمَدِيْنَةُ شِرَارَهَا،

186
00:13:11,988 --> 00:13:13,702
 كَمَا يَنْفِيْ الْكِيْرُ خَبَثَ الْحَدِيْدِ

187
00:13:13,742 --> 00:13:17,824
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; in Muslim(مسلم) in the name of whom, My soul is in his hands,

188
00:13:17,996 --> 00:13:22,052
Nobody leaves Madina because he doesn't want it anymore,

189
00:13:22,333 --> 00:13:25,754
except that Allah will replace him with someone better than him.

190
00:13:26,091 --> 00:13:27,589
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ says,

191
00:13:28,114 --> 00:13:33,458
that Madina cleanses itself from the people, who are impure or the people who are evil.

192
00:13:34,107 --> 00:13:40,732
And Rasool Allah ﷺ says the day of judgment will not occur until Madina drives out all of the evil people in it,

193
00:13:41,658 --> 00:13:44,505
like the fire would drive out the impurities of iron.

194
00:13:45,438 --> 00:13:47,522
Allahعَزّوجَلّ protects Madina,

195
00:13:47,698 --> 00:13:48,706
 Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

196
00:13:48,799 --> 00:13:54,229
لا يَكِيدُ أهْلَ المَدِينَةِ أحَدٌ، إلَّا انْمَاعَ كما يَنْمَاعُ المِلْحُ في المَاءِ

197
00:13:54,638 --> 00:13:59,416
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; Whoever plots against the people of Madina,

198
00:13:59,456 --> 00:14:03,124
Allah will make him dissolve like salt dissolves in water.

199
00:14:03,383 --> 00:14:04,818
This Hadith(حديث) is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

200
00:14:05,052 --> 00:14:07,193
And Madina also is sacred.

201
00:14:07,973 --> 00:14:10,974
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ says, you're not allowed to cut down trees in Madina,

202
00:14:11,165 --> 00:14:12,831
you're not allowed to hunt in Madina,

203
00:14:12,993 --> 00:14:17,713
you're not allowed to carry weapons in Madina, because of its sanctity.

204
00:14:18,322 --> 00:14:22,893
So, these are some of the blessings of the Madina of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

205
00:14:24,518 --> 00:14:29,222
Before Rasool Allah ﷺ decided to make Hijrah(هجرة), the people of Makkah plotted against him,

206
00:14:29,549 --> 00:14:34,634
they came together, and they started discussing how to deal with the Islamic problem.

207
00:14:35,534 --> 00:14:39,509
Some of them suggested that we should throw Muhammadﷺ in jail,

208
00:14:40,474 --> 00:14:43,322
the response was no, don't do that this is not a good idea.

209
00:14:43,369 --> 00:14:46,785
Because if you throw him in jail, his followers will come and take him out,

210
00:14:47,610 --> 00:14:49,205
they're going to revolt against us.

211
00:14:49,634 --> 00:14:55,204
So, the second suggestion came in and that's to exile, drive them out of Madina.

212
00:14:55,664 --> 00:14:58,997
 So, they said no, that's not a good idea, because his talk is very sweet.

213
00:14:59,418 --> 00:15:01,845
 So, he's going to deceive other people to believe in him,

214
00:15:01,997 --> 00:15:04,138
and then they're going to come back to you again.

215
00:15:04,966 --> 00:15:09,629
So, the third suggestion was that of obviously who else other than Abu Jahal(أبو جهل),

216
00:15:10,161 --> 00:15:12,192
 he said, we should kill him.

217
00:15:12,474 --> 00:15:17,677
And the way to do that is to appoint a strong man from every clan, give him a sharp sword,

218
00:15:18,334 --> 00:15:21,739
and then have them all strike Muhammad(محمد) at once,

219
00:15:22,488 --> 00:15:26,562
so that his blood will disperse among the different clans of Makkah,

220
00:15:26,951 --> 00:15:30,261
so that the family of Rasool Allah ﷺ will not be able to seek revenge.

221
00:15:30,620 --> 00:15:34,370
And then they will ask for blood money and we will be happy to pay it, to them.

222
00:15:35,425 --> 00:15:37,692
They said: This is the suggestion that we adopt.

223
00:15:37,872 --> 00:15:39,552
 And Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

224
00:15:39,826 --> 00:15:47,953
وَإِذْ يَمْكُرُ بِكَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا لِيُثْبِتُوكَ أَوْ يَقْتُلُوكَ أَوْ يُخْرِجُوكَ ۚ

225
00:15:48,421 --> 00:15:54,599
وَيَمْكُرُونَ وَيَمْكُرُ اللَّهُ ۖ وَاللَّهُ خَيْرُ الْمَاكِرِينَ۝

226
00:15:54,806 --> 00:15:56,134
And remember O Muhammad(محمد),

227
00:15:56,629 --> 00:16:02,444
when those who disbelieved plotted against you, to restrain you, which is, to throw you in jail,

228
00:16:02,650 --> 00:16:06,024
 or to kill you, or to evict you from Makkah,

229
00:16:06,381 --> 00:16:10,118
 but they plan and Allah plans and Allah is the best of planners.

230
00:16:11,346 --> 00:16:14,745
So, they planned to execute Muhammadﷺ.

231
00:16:15,726 --> 00:16:19,463
They wanted to assassinate him, but Allahعَزّوجَلّ will protect him.

232
00:16:20,152 --> 00:16:26,385
Allahعَزّوجَلّ told Muhammadﷺ to recite the following Dua(دُعَا) and this is an Ayah(آية) in Surat Al-Israa(إسرآء).

233
00:16:26,718 --> 00:16:39,618
وَقُلْ رَبِّ أَدْخِلْنِي مُدْخَلَ صِدْقٍ وَأَخْرِجْنِي مُخْرَجَ صِدْقٍ وَاجْعَلْ لِي مِنْ لَدُنْكَ سُلْطَانًا نَصِيرًا۝

234
00:16:40,843 --> 00:16:45,465
And say my Lord cause me to enter a sound entrance,

235
00:16:45,882 --> 00:16:50,889
and to exit a sound exit, and grant me from yourself a supporting authority.

236
00:16:51,944 --> 00:16:55,739
So, to cause me to enter a sound entrance is to go to Madina,

237
00:16:56,321 --> 00:16:58,728
and to exit the sound exit is to leave Makkah

238
00:16:59,457 --> 00:17:02,336
and grant me from yourself a supporting authority,

239
00:17:02,376 --> 00:17:06,145
because Allahعَزّوجَلّ is teaching Muhammad(محمد) that this religion is supported by authority.

240
00:17:06,619 --> 00:17:13,327
Rasool Allah ﷺ says that Allahعَزّوجَلّ, sometimes could support this religion through authority in ways that

241
00:17:13,910 --> 00:17:16,553
Qur'an(قرآن) cannot support the religion

242
00:17:17,361 --> 00:17:21,124
and that's why Khilafah(خِلَافَه) was a very important concept to the Muslims.

243
00:17:22,582 --> 00:17:27,725
In fact, the Sahabah(صحابه) met to decide the issue of Khalifah(خليفه) before they buried Rasool Allah ﷺ,

244
00:17:28,494 --> 00:17:31,475
as we mentioned in the story of Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه.

245
00:17:31,905 --> 00:17:34,887
Rasool Allah ﷺ set out to prepare for Hijrah(هجرة),

246
00:17:35,369 --> 00:17:41,217
Ayeshaرضي الله عنها said, that one day at mid noon, in the house of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر),

247
00:17:41,471 --> 00:17:46,814
 we saw a man approaching us and he was masked, he covered his face.

248
00:17:47,556 --> 00:17:50,557
So, Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابو بكر الصديق) saw that it was Muhammadﷺ.

249
00:17:50,582 --> 00:17:53,819
 He said: Muhammadﷺ wouldn't come at this time, except if it's something important.

250
00:17:54,870 --> 00:17:57,765
Because it was at noon people usually sleep at noon.

251
00:17:59,245 --> 00:18:00,756
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ came in.

252
00:18:01,065 --> 00:18:04,921
And he said: O Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), have everyone in your house, leave.

253
00:18:06,250 --> 00:18:08,009
Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه said;

254
00:18:08,474 --> 00:18:11,588
the only ones, who are in my house are your family, O Rasool Ullah!

255
00:18:11,667 --> 00:18:13,147
Meaning my family is like yours.

256
00:18:13,947 --> 00:18:18,066
You can trust speaking in the presence of my family because they are like your own family.

257
00:18:18,808 --> 00:18:25,488
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I was given permission to leave and to make Hijrah(هجرة) to Madina.

258
00:18:25,650 --> 00:18:27,708
Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه said;

259
00:18:27,795 --> 00:18:31,836
 O Messenger of Allah Can I be your companion?

260
00:18:32,213 --> 00:18:33,813
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: yes.

261
00:18:34,101 --> 00:18:36,718
Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه started to weep.

262
00:18:37,252 --> 00:18:38,612
Ayeshaرضي الله عنها said;

263
00:18:38,660 --> 00:18:44,966
I never saw somebody weeping because of pleasure, because of joy, like my father that day.

264
00:18:45,719 --> 00:18:48,306
Now, I just want to stop right here and say,

265
00:18:49,335 --> 00:18:51,275
this was not an entertaining journey.

266
00:18:52,747 --> 00:18:58,315
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) knew very well, that is risking his life by being the companion of Rasool Allah ﷺ on Hijrah(هجرة).

267
00:18:59,283 --> 00:19:02,421
So, how come he is crying of joy?

268
00:19:03,215 --> 00:19:05,876
When he knows that he's putting his life on the line.

269
00:19:07,095 --> 00:19:13,457
Brothers and sisters, this shows you the level of sacrifice that Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه is willing to go to,

270
00:19:13,839 --> 00:19:17,699
and it shows you that he's so happy to sacrifice for Rasool Allah ﷺ.

271
00:19:17,783 --> 00:19:19,984
I mean, his heart is not trembling, he's not afraid.

272
00:19:20,346 --> 00:19:25,405
He's crying because of joy, when he knows that he could be killed.

273
00:19:26,905 --> 00:19:31,241
But this shows you, the love that he had, for Rasool Allah ﷺ.

274
00:19:32,296 --> 00:19:35,782
Rasool Ullah appointed Ali Ibn Abi Talib(عليابن ابي طالب) to sleep on his bed

275
00:19:35,794 --> 00:19:38,950
and this is another sacrifice because Ali Ibn AbiTalib(علي ابن ابي طالب) was also risking his life.

276
00:19:40,080 --> 00:19:44,026
But these were the Sahabah(صحابه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ, this is how far they were willing to go.

277
00:19:44,559 --> 00:19:47,114
Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), they left Makkah

278
00:19:47,971 --> 00:19:51,066
and Rasool Allah loved Makkah so much.

279
00:19:51,281 --> 00:19:53,670
So, he looked back and he said;

280
00:19:53,710 --> 00:19:58,797
 وَلله اِنَّكِيْ لَخَيْرُ اَرْضِ الله وَاَحَبُّ اَرْضِاللهِ اِلَى الله،

281
00:19:59,232 --> 00:20:02,002
وَلَوْ لَا اَنِّيْ اُخْرِجْتُ مِنْكِيْ مَا خَرَجْت

282
00:20:02,481 --> 00:20:07,416
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: In the name of Allah, you are the most beloved land to Allah.

283
00:20:08,461 --> 00:20:13,165
And if it wasn't that I was driven out from you, I wouldn't have left.

284
00:20:13,784 --> 00:20:18,609
I wouldn't leave Makkah, if I had the choice, but he was driven out of it.

285
00:20:20,334 --> 00:20:26,797
The journey started and Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه for some time would walk ahead of Rasool Ullah,

286
00:20:28,008 --> 00:20:30,834
and then for some time, he would walk behind Rasool Ullah.

287
00:20:32,149 --> 00:20:34,798
So, the Messenger of Allah noticed that and then he asked Abu Bakr(ابو بكر),

288
00:20:34,822 --> 00:20:39,874
how come sometimes you walk in front of me and sometimes you walk behind me?

289
00:20:41,118 --> 00:20:42,981
Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه said;

290
00:20:43,384 --> 00:20:48,121
When I remembered that somebody could ambush you from in front of us,

291
00:20:48,355 --> 00:20:49,395
I walk ahead of you

292
00:20:49,863 --> 00:20:53,522
and then I remember that somebody could be pursuing us, so I walked behind you.

293
00:20:54,448 --> 00:20:56,362
Then Rasool Allah ﷺ said: O Abu Bakr(ابو بكر)

294
00:20:57,053 --> 00:21:00,321
would you rather have harm happened to you or to me.?

295
00:21:01,271 --> 00:21:06,857
Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه said: O Messenger of Allah, I would rather have it, happened to me and not to you.

296
00:21:07,912 --> 00:21:12,083
And then they reach to the cave, so Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه went into check the cave

297
00:21:12,107 --> 00:21:16,519
to make sure that there's no snakes, there's no scorpions, there's no ambush.

298
00:21:17,701 --> 00:21:19,354
And then he told Rasool Allah ﷺ to come in.

299
00:21:20,279 --> 00:21:22,766
When they were in the cave, the Kuffar(كفار) of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

300
00:21:23,352 --> 00:21:25,473
succeeded in following their tracks

301
00:21:25,735 --> 00:21:28,069
until they reached to the mouth of the cave.

302
00:21:29,198 --> 00:21:32,251
Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه told Rasool Allah ﷺ,

303
00:21:32,291 --> 00:21:33,291
يا رسول الله

304
00:21:33,394 --> 00:21:34,799
O Messenger of Allah,

305
00:21:35,240 --> 00:21:40,748
if one of them would stare right under their feet, they would see us,

306
00:21:42,584 --> 00:21:44,992
they were right there at the mouth of the cave.

307
00:21:45,839 --> 00:21:48,366
Rasool Allah ﷺ with all confidence. He said;

308
00:21:48,477 --> 00:21:49,390
يَا اَبَا بَكْر

309
00:21:49,899 --> 00:21:55,538
O Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), What do you think about two men, if Allah is their third.

310
00:21:56,205 --> 00:21:59,477
مَا ظَنُّكَ بِاثْنَيْنْ الله ثَالِثُهُمَا

311
00:21:59,528 --> 00:22:02,714
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), how would you regard the safety of two people,

312
00:22:02,953 --> 00:22:05,435
who had Allah, as their third companion.

313
00:22:06,347 --> 00:22:08,297
You know what stop them from entering the cave.?

314
00:22:09,218 --> 00:22:10,718
 It was a web of a spider.

315
00:22:11,311 --> 00:22:14,127
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says about the web of the spider.

316
00:22:14,268 --> 00:22:17,485
وَإنَّ أَوْهَنَ الْبُيُوتِ لَبَيْتُ الْعَنكَبُوتِ

317
00:22:17,954 --> 00:22:22,016
The most feeble of houses, is the house of a spider

318
00:22:22,628 --> 00:22:26,157
with one finger you could tear down the whole web.

319
00:22:27,706 --> 00:22:29,881
So, this feeble weak web

320
00:22:30,779 --> 00:22:35,818
was the soldier of Allah, that stopped the disbelievers from entering into the cave.

321
00:22:36,743 --> 00:22:42,643
And this shows us that Allahعَزّوجَلّ can choose sometimes the weakest of His creation, to be His soldier.

322
00:22:44,112 --> 00:22:48,474
This story of the web of the spider is an agreeable narration, it is Hassan(حسن).

323
00:22:49,373 --> 00:22:50,779
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

324
00:22:51,247 --> 00:22:54,636
If you do not aid him, Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed this Ayah(آية) later on.

325
00:22:54,660 --> 00:22:58,887
This Ayah(آية) is in Surat-Taubah(سورةالتوبة), it's few years after the Hijrah(هجرة).

326
00:22:59,629 --> 00:23:02,127
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ is speaking to the Sahabah(صحابه) and telling them

327
00:23:02,471 --> 00:23:05,938
if you do not aid him, Allah has already aided him.

328
00:23:06,460 --> 00:23:11,973
You know, that day when Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) was the only companion of Rasool Allah ﷺ

329
00:23:12,131 --> 00:23:14,100
and the Kuffar(كفار) were surrounding the cave,

330
00:23:14,385 --> 00:23:17,851
none of you were around and Allah didn't need you to support His Prophet.

331
00:23:18,484 --> 00:23:22,864
So, Allah is telling the Sahabah(صحابه), if you do not aid him now, Allah has already aided him.

332
00:23:23,249 --> 00:23:28,979
إِلَّا تَنْصُرُوهُ فَقَدْ نَصَرَهُ اللَّهُ

333
00:23:29,447 --> 00:23:39,015
إِذْ أَخْرَجَهُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا ثَانِيَ اثْنَيْنِ إِذْ هُمَا فِي الْغَارِ إِذْ يَقُولُ لِصَاحِبِهِ

334
00:23:39,499 --> 00:23:46,689
 إِذْ يَقُولُ لِصَاحِبِهِ لَا تَحْزَنْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَنَا

335
00:23:47,090 --> 00:23:55,899
 فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ سَكِينَتَهُ عَلَيْهِ وَأَيَّدَهُ بِجُنُودٍ لَمْ تَرَوْهَا

336
00:23:56,152 --> 00:24:03,851
وَجَعَلَ كَلِمَةَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا السُّفْلَىٰ ۗ وَكَلِمَةُ اللَّهِ هِيَ الْعُلْيَا ۗ

337
00:24:04,208 --> 00:24:07,748
وَاللَّهُ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ۝

338
00:24:08,119 --> 00:24:12,390
When those, who believed had driven him out as one of two

339
00:24:13,574 --> 00:24:16,361
when they were in the cave, and he said to his companion.

340
00:24:16,385 --> 00:24:20,381
So notice here, Allah is calling Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) as the companion of Rasool Allah,

341
00:24:20,444 --> 00:24:22,944
that's an honor to Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه,

342
00:24:23,036 --> 00:24:23,714
لِصَاحِبِهِ

343
00:24:23,960 --> 00:24:24,571
his companion.

344
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:31,552
Do not grieve indeed Allah is with us and Allah sent down his tranquility upon him,

345
00:24:32,073 --> 00:24:34,845
and supported him with soldiers, you did not see.

346
00:24:35,710 --> 00:24:37,424
One of these soldiers is a spider,

347
00:24:38,089 --> 00:24:44,508
and made the word of those who disbelieved the lowest while the word of Allah that is the highest

348
00:24:44,911 --> 00:24:46,899
and Allah is exalted in Might and Wise.

349
00:24:47,011 --> 00:24:49,693
So, the soldiers of Allah referred to in this Ayaah(آية) are the angels.

350
00:24:50,011 --> 00:24:51,534
These are the unseen soldiers.

351
00:24:51,849 --> 00:24:54,760
But then you also have the spider, which was a seen soldier.

352
00:24:56,888 --> 00:24:59,609
Now, they stayed in the cave for three days,

353
00:25:01,041 --> 00:25:06,694
during those three days, Abdullah(عبدالله) the son of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) would spend a day in Makkah,

354
00:25:07,512 --> 00:25:11,083
listening to conversations ears dropping,

355
00:25:11,797 --> 00:25:14,903
to see what they're saying about Muhammadﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر),

356
00:25:15,625 --> 00:25:20,839
and then he would go at night and spend it with Rasool Allah and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) in the cave.

357
00:25:22,292 --> 00:25:28,320
And he would have Aamir Bin Fuhairah(عامربن فحيرة), the servant of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) follow him with his sheep.

358
00:25:29,349 --> 00:25:30,456
So, this has a double purpose

359
00:25:31,068 --> 00:25:35,221
the sheep will provide milk to the prophet and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر).

360
00:25:35,781 --> 00:25:40,482
And the sheep will also cover the tracks of Abdullah(عبدالله) and Aamir(عامر),

361
00:25:41,120 --> 00:25:44,043
so that no one will know, where they went,

362
00:25:45,729 --> 00:25:47,487
and this carried on for three days.

363
00:25:48,099 --> 00:25:53,190
And then the guide showed up, which was Abdullah Bin Uraiqat(عبد الله بن اريقط),

364
00:25:53,776 --> 00:26:01,081
he was a Mushrik(مشرك) a disbeliever, but because he had an alliance with people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

365
00:26:01,628 --> 00:26:04,115
Rasool Allah ﷺ hired him to be their guide.

366
00:26:05,638 --> 00:26:12,443
So, he was the one, who will take them through a different route than the usual one that people usually take.

367
00:26:12,774 --> 00:26:14,349
When they travel from Makkah to Madina.

368
00:26:16,496 --> 00:26:21,797
They set on, the trip to Madina,

369
00:26:22,591 --> 00:26:28,904
they did not follow the regular route, but they went on the coast, coastline.

370
00:26:29,214 --> 00:26:32,436
They followed the coastline, until they reached to Madina.

371
00:26:33,711 --> 00:26:38,412
The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) set a bounty on Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر),

372
00:26:38,929 --> 00:26:41,400
100 camels each dead or alive.

373
00:26:42,113 --> 00:26:46,191
And they were sending out their messengers to convey the news to the Bedouins of the desert.

374
00:26:46,675 --> 00:26:49,524
The experts of the routes of the desert

375
00:26:49,945 --> 00:26:56,482
telling them that, bring us Muhammadﷺ, Dead or Alive or Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) we'll give you 100 camels each.

376
00:26:57,308 --> 00:27:02,591
Suraqah Bin Malik(سُراقه بن مالك) was the head of one of these Bedouin tribes.

377
00:27:03,155 --> 00:27:05,794
He said, I was sitting in a gathering of my people,

378
00:27:06,468 --> 00:27:12,934
when a man showed up and said, I saw two men in the horizon.

379
00:27:13,370 --> 00:27:16,716
And I think that these are the two men Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) are looking for!

380
00:27:17,643 --> 00:27:22,575
Suraqah(سُراقه) said, I told him, No, these two men were just here a while ago and they just left.

381
00:27:23,464 --> 00:27:26,125
He said, I told them that to deceive him,

382
00:27:26,308 --> 00:27:30,859
but I knew or I felt that those men were Muhammadﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر),

383
00:27:31,316 --> 00:27:35,496
but I just told him that because I wanted to get the camels for myself.

384
00:27:36,022 --> 00:27:39,880
So, Suraqah(سُراقه) said, I stayed in the gathering for a while so that they wouldn't be suspicious.

385
00:27:40,661 --> 00:27:47,366
And then I left, I went to my house and I told my servant to go and prepare my horse, the saddle and all

386
00:27:47,694 --> 00:27:51,081
 and to hide it behind a mountain or a hill.

387
00:27:51,784 --> 00:27:57,553
And I left from the back door, and I was carrying my spear and he said my spear was dragging on the ground.

388
00:27:58,198 --> 00:28:04,048
Why? Because spear is long, so he didn't want anybody to see it, so he was dragging it.

389
00:28:04,644 --> 00:28:10,586
And then he said I mounted my horse and I went to the direction that, that man saw the two men.

390
00:28:11,396 --> 00:28:15,640
And it was as I thought the two men were Muhammadﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر).

391
00:28:16,782 --> 00:28:20,875
So, now you only have a few meters between Suraqah(سراقه) becoming a millionaire,

392
00:28:21,685 --> 00:28:24,867
one hundred camels each, he's right there.

393
00:28:25,433 --> 00:28:27,251
Suraqah(سراقه) says; Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) was looking back,

394
00:28:27,854 --> 00:28:31,008
while Muhammadﷺ was reciting Qur'an and he never looked back.

395
00:28:31,672 --> 00:28:36,317
Rasool Allah ﷺ was confident that Allahعَزّوجَلّ will give him victory, while Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) was very concerned,

396
00:28:36,740 --> 00:28:39,498
not for himself but concerned for the safety of Muhammadﷺ.

397
00:28:39,538 --> 00:28:42,765
So, he was staring back, while Muhammadﷺ was reciting Qur'an.

398
00:28:43,399 --> 00:28:46,254
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) told Rasool Allah ﷺ that somebody pursuing us,

399
00:28:47,345 --> 00:28:53,184
Rasool Allah ﷺ made a Dua(دُعَا) and the horse of Suraqah(سُراقه) sank in the sand,

400
00:28:53,863 --> 00:28:55,802
and Suraqah(سُراقه) fell off his back.

401
00:28:56,646 --> 00:29:01,870
Suraqah(سُراقه) said: So, I cast lots, you know, they had all of these superstitious beliefs.

402
00:29:03,423 --> 00:29:06,167
He cast lots, Should I follow them or shouldn't I follow them?

403
00:29:07,250 --> 00:29:09,289
The Lots told me that I shouldn't follow them.

404
00:29:09,718 --> 00:29:13,501
But I insisted on following them, his greed, drived him further.

405
00:29:13,823 --> 00:29:17,442
So, what's the point of casting the lots, if you're going to disobey them anyway,

406
00:29:18,410 --> 00:29:21,558
he followed them, another time and the same thing happened.

407
00:29:22,319 --> 00:29:26,300
He fell off his horse and he said, This never happened to me, I never fell off my horse

408
00:29:27,124 --> 00:29:28,919
The third time it happened to him.

409
00:29:29,173 --> 00:29:36,769
He said a cloud of dust exploded in my face from in front of my horse.

410
00:29:37,173 --> 00:29:40,346
 So, I knew that Allah supporting this man,

411
00:29:41,074 --> 00:29:44,731
so I rushed towards him asking him to grant me peace.

412
00:29:45,767 --> 00:29:49,976
Suraqah(سُراقه), who was pursuing Muhammadﷺ now became the pursuit.

413
00:29:50,464 --> 00:29:55,876
Suraqah(سُراقه) who thought that he could kill Muhammadﷺ is now worried for his own safety

414
00:29:55,956 --> 00:29:58,569
and he's asking Muhammadﷺ to grant him peace.

415
00:30:00,112 --> 00:30:02,410
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told him; I grant you peace.

416
00:30:02,450 --> 00:30:05,389
Suraqah(سُراقه) told him, write that down for me on a piece of paper.

417
00:30:05,499 --> 00:30:07,514
I want to make sure write it down for me.

418
00:30:07,785 --> 00:30:09,665
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told Aamir Bin Fuhairah(عامربن فحيرة)

419
00:30:09,761 --> 00:30:15,193
to write down a document stating that Rasool Allah ﷺ is granting Suraqah Bin Malik(سُراقه بن مالك) peace.

420
00:30:16,812 --> 00:30:22,203
Suraqah(سُراقه) sticks this piece of cloth or whatever in his pocket, and years passed by.

421
00:30:23,537 --> 00:30:29,101
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) eight or nine years later, he was arrested.

422
00:30:29,897 --> 00:30:33,371
When Rasool Allah ﷺ was laying siege to At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف)

423
00:30:34,308 --> 00:30:36,746
and when they were going to kill him.

424
00:30:36,842 --> 00:30:43,445
 He pulled that document out and he told them this is a paper a document from Rasool Allah ﷺ granting me peace,

425
00:30:43,886 --> 00:30:46,271
that document saved his life.

426
00:30:47,167 --> 00:30:48,212
Now Suraqah(سُراقه) went back

427
00:30:49,003 --> 00:30:55,458
and he told the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) that you're not gonna find Muhammadﷺ, forget about it.

428
00:30:56,484 --> 00:31:01,513
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ told him, to weaken anybody who's trying to pursue us,

429
00:31:02,138 --> 00:31:03,359
drive them away from us.

430
00:31:03,462 --> 00:31:10,286
So, Suraqah(سراقه) who was trying to arrest them now, is their guard,

431
00:31:11,241 --> 00:31:15,223
Suraqah(سراقه) became a bodyguard for Muhammadﷺ.

432
00:31:17,322 --> 00:31:22,293
Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), visited a tent

433
00:31:23,486 --> 00:31:28,038
In front of this tent was a woman, an old woman, her name is Ummo Ma'abad(أم معبد).

434
00:31:29,140 --> 00:31:32,782
This was a very generous woman, anybody who would pass by, she would feed them.

435
00:31:33,320 --> 00:31:37,277
When Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) got there, she didn't provide them with anything.

436
00:31:38,515 --> 00:31:42,475
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ asked her if she has anything to spare.

437
00:31:42,745 --> 00:31:45,423
She said: If I had anything you wouldn't have to ask.

438
00:31:46,405 --> 00:31:51,786
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ saw in the corner of her tent a very weak goat.

439
00:31:52,792 --> 00:31:54,850
So, he asked her: what's the problem with that goat?

440
00:31:54,930 --> 00:32:00,811
She said, that goat is too weak to go out with the rest of the flock, to feed.

441
00:32:01,629 --> 00:32:04,881
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Is there any milk in her?

442
00:32:05,222 --> 00:32:07,010
She said she's weaker than that.

443
00:32:07,541 --> 00:32:09,739
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Will you allow me to milk her,

444
00:32:09,779 --> 00:32:10,842
She said: Go ahead.

445
00:32:11,873 --> 00:32:17,215
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ goes to milk that goat and he asks for a big container, not a cup, a big container.

446
00:32:18,059 --> 00:32:21,598
And then he touches the goat and he starts milking it.

447
00:32:22,273 --> 00:32:28,953
And milk is flowing out, until it fills the container, and all of this foam on top of the milk.

448
00:32:30,076 --> 00:32:32,219
And then he gives it to Ummo Ma'abad(أم معبد) first.

449
00:32:32,441 --> 00:32:33,346
So, she drinks

450
00:32:34,157 --> 00:32:38,665
and then he gives it to Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) and Aamir(عامر) and Abdullah Bin Uraiqat(عبدالله بن اريقط), they all drink

451
00:32:38,705 --> 00:32:43,272
 and he's the last to drink and he said the servant of the people is the last to drink.

452
00:32:43,835 --> 00:32:45,161
So, he was the last to drink.

453
00:32:45,701 --> 00:32:48,778
And then he left and there was still a lot of milk in that container.

454
00:32:49,354 --> 00:32:53,211
So, the husband of Umm Ma'abad(أم معبد) comes back with the flock, with his flock of sheep.

455
00:32:53,963 --> 00:32:57,684
And he sees this milk and he says Ummo Ma'abad(أم معبد), where does, this milk come from?

456
00:32:58,592 --> 00:33:01,087
She said: A blessed man, visited us.

457
00:33:02,147 --> 00:33:06,160
And he's the one, who milked the she goat.

458
00:33:07,049 --> 00:33:09,461
He asked her to describe this man to her.

459
00:33:10,876 --> 00:33:13,602
Umm Ma'abad(أم معبد) gave a description of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

460
00:33:13,642 --> 00:33:18,563
that remains, until this day as one of the best descriptions ever given about Rasool Allah ﷺ,

461
00:33:18,762 --> 00:33:20,516
even though she only met him once.

462
00:33:21,407 --> 00:33:25,547
And I will read to you her description of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

463
00:33:26,148 --> 00:33:30,318
She said: I saw him to be a man of evident splendor,

464
00:33:31,183 --> 00:33:32,319
fine in figure,

465
00:33:32,700 --> 00:33:36,046
his face handsome, slim in form,

466
00:33:36,906 --> 00:33:41,193
his head not too small, elegant and good looking,

467
00:33:42,169 --> 00:33:44,054
his eyes large and black,

468
00:33:45,275 --> 00:33:48,292
his eyelids long his voice deep,

469
00:33:49,064 --> 00:33:50,135
very intelligent,

470
00:33:50,802 --> 00:33:52,652
his bros high and arched,

471
00:33:53,410 --> 00:33:58,331
his hair in plates, his neck long and his beard thick.

472
00:33:59,376 --> 00:34:01,554
He gave an impression of dignity when silent

473
00:34:02,086 --> 00:34:04,317
and of high intelligence when he talked.

474
00:34:04,933 --> 00:34:06,360
His words were impressive.

475
00:34:06,638 --> 00:34:09,662
And he was decisive, not trivial, not trite.

476
00:34:10,167 --> 00:34:13,205
His ideas like pearls moving on their string.

477
00:34:14,249 --> 00:34:17,804
He seemed the most splendid and fine looking man from a distance

478
00:34:18,537 --> 00:34:21,445
and the very best of all from close by,

479
00:34:22,088 --> 00:34:23,223
medium and height.

480
00:34:23,634 --> 00:34:26,417
The eye not finding him too tall nor too short.

481
00:34:27,111 --> 00:34:29,866
tree branch as it were, between two others,

482
00:34:30,059 --> 00:34:32,297
but he was the finest looking of the three.

483
00:34:33,186 --> 00:34:34,543
The best proportioned,

484
00:34:35,448 --> 00:34:38,259
he was the center of his companions attention.

485
00:34:38,585 --> 00:34:40,451
When he spoke they listened well.

486
00:34:40,761 --> 00:34:43,666
And if he ordered the hurried to obey,

487
00:34:44,023 --> 00:34:48,585
a man well helped, well served, never solemn, never refuted.

488
00:34:50,180 --> 00:34:51,205
 Her husband said;

489
00:34:51,496 --> 00:34:56,910
this man must be Muhammad(محمد), the one whom Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) are pursuing.

490
00:34:57,219 --> 00:34:58,164
If I meet him.

491
00:34:58,530 --> 00:35:01,006
I will pledge allegiance to him and become Muslim.

492
00:35:02,442 --> 00:35:07,112
Now by the way, Ummo Ma'abad(أم معبد) did pledge allegiance to Rasool Allah ﷺ and she became Muslim.

493
00:35:08,693 --> 00:35:10,426
Some lessons from Hijrah(هجرة).

494
00:35:11,251 --> 00:35:12,916
Number one, the concept of Hijrah(هجرة).

495
00:35:13,305 --> 00:35:14,734
There are two types of Hijrah(هجرة).

496
00:35:15,724 --> 00:35:18,507
There's figurative Hijrah(هجرة) and there's the literal Hijrah(هجرة).

497
00:35:20,021 --> 00:35:27,150
The figurative Hijrah(هجرة) is as was mentioned in a Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ in An-Nasae(ألنسائ)

498
00:35:27,609 --> 00:35:30,958
أَنْ تَهْجُرَ مَا كَرِهَ رَبُّكَ عَزّ وجَل

499
00:35:32,433 --> 00:35:37,870
Hijrah(هجرة) is to leave what Allahعَزّوجَلّ dislikes.

500
00:35:39,073 --> 00:35:46,501
So, this is a figurative Hijrah(هجرة), it is to emigrate from the state of sin to the state of obeying Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

501
00:35:47,740 --> 00:35:48,936
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ says in Qur'an

502
00:35:48,960 --> 00:35:50,287
وَالرُّجْزَ فَاهْجُرْ

503
00:35:50,501 --> 00:35:51,827
Stay away from impurities,

504
00:35:51,908 --> 00:35:57,035
make Hijrah(هجرة) from impurities from idol worshipping from evil.

505
00:35:58,412 --> 00:36:01,063
And this type of Hijrah(هجرة) is mandatory on everyone.

506
00:36:01,908 --> 00:36:06,155
All of us have to leave the state of sin, to the state of obedience.

507
00:36:06,927 --> 00:36:10,660
Then we have the literal Hijrah(هجرة) and that is to move from one land to another,

508
00:36:10,700 --> 00:36:13,671
you loof from the land of evil to the land of good.

509
00:36:13,959 --> 00:36:17,189
Examples of that are the Hijrah(هجرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Sahabah(صحابه),

510
00:36:17,539 --> 00:36:21,454
or the Hijrah(هجرة) of the man from the children of Israel(اسرائيل) who killed 100 people.

511
00:36:21,913 --> 00:36:23,400
And then he went to consult the scholars.

512
00:36:23,478 --> 00:36:29,032
So, the scholar told him, Allah will accept your repentance, but you have to move from this town.

513
00:36:29,780 --> 00:36:32,408
Because it's the town of evil and go to that other town

514
00:36:32,433 --> 00:36:36,726
because you'll find there in people who will support you, in worshipping Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

515
00:36:37,948 --> 00:36:39,083
Benefits of Hijrah(هجرة).

516
00:36:39,687 --> 00:36:41,746
Hijrah(هجرة) can cause an economic boom.

517
00:36:43,103 --> 00:36:44,365
Examples of that,

518
00:36:44,912 --> 00:36:52,072
Grenada, for example, Grenada, the Muslim Grenada at the last Islamic state, in Andalusia(أندلسيه),

519
00:36:52,366 --> 00:36:59,619
 when the Christian north, the Spaniards started taking over conquering Islamic land

520
00:37:00,137 --> 00:37:05,342
the Muslims would leave, and they would settle in southern Spain in Grenada(غرناطه).

521
00:37:06,426 --> 00:37:10,244
So, there was a population boom, it reached to over 2 million.

522
00:37:11,055 --> 00:37:16,670
But these are men, who came in with their skills with their abilities as merchants,

523
00:37:17,196 --> 00:37:19,452
their abilities as farmers.

524
00:37:20,127 --> 00:37:25,821
So, Grenada flourished and it became the wealthiest state in all of Europe.

525
00:37:26,905 --> 00:37:33,653
What caused that, major part was due to the Hijrah(هجرة) of the Muslims from northern Spain, to the southern Spain.

526
00:37:34,385 --> 00:37:37,383
