00:50:39,397 --> 00:50:41,592
he didn't want to tell them that this is Muhammadﷺ,

717
00:50:41,632 --> 00:50:45,105
because now you have 100 camels, there was a bounty on Rasool Allah ﷺ.

718
00:50:45,584 --> 00:50:51,140
So, he wanted to protect his identity and the way he did it, was by making the statement.

719
00:50:51,180 --> 00:50:53,723
So, you can see that Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) is not lying.

720
00:50:54,705 --> 00:50:58,685
But they are understanding something different than what he means.

721
00:50:59,832 --> 00:51:04,363
This is, what is called Toriah(توريه), so you can see this secrecy part.

722
00:51:04,648 --> 00:51:05,935
Now when it comes to Da'wah(دعوة),

723
00:51:06,841 --> 00:51:11,479
the identity would need to be exposed for Da'wah(دعوة), so when Rasool Allah ﷺ met with Buraid Al Aslami(بريد الأسلمي).

724
00:51:11,883 --> 00:51:17,166
He did, tell him that I am Muhammadﷺ and he did give him Da'wah(دعوة) and Buraidah(بريدة) became Muslim.

725
00:51:17,675 --> 00:51:21,477
And he joined Rasool Allah ﷺ in the 16 out of his 19 battles.

726
00:51:21,830 --> 00:51:23,649
And he was ahead of his people.

727
00:51:24,671 --> 00:51:27,605
Rasool Allah ﷺ also met with two thieves,

728
00:51:28,006 --> 00:51:30,691
and he gave them Da'wah(دعوة) and they became Muslim.

729
00:51:31,551 --> 00:51:34,191
Rasool Allah ﷺ said, What's your name?

730
00:51:34,231 --> 00:51:37,228
They said: Our name is the Al-Muhanaan(ألمهانان),

731
00:51:37,488 --> 00:51:39,768
Al-Muhanaan(ألمهانان) means the dishonored ones.

732
00:51:40,252 --> 00:51:42,351
The people used to call them the dishonored ones.

733
00:51:42,409 --> 00:51:44,849
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told them, No, you are the honored ones.

734
00:51:46,385 --> 00:51:49,988
Another example of Da'wah(دعوة) Rasool Allah ﷺ met with a shepherd.

735
00:51:50,603 --> 00:51:57,039
So, he asked him; Can you give us some milk, the shepherd said none of my goats has milk at the moment.

736
00:51:57,732 --> 00:52:01,141
Rasool Allah ﷺ chose one of them and said would you allow me to milk it?

737
00:52:01,696 --> 00:52:06,414
The shepherd said; Go ahead and Rasool Allah ﷺ did milk it and a lot of milk started flowing out.

738
00:52:06,912 --> 00:52:12,055
And then he gave the shepherd to drink first and then He and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) drank.

739
00:52:12,401 --> 00:52:15,741
So, the shepherd asked Muhammadﷺ, he said;

740
00:52:16,228 --> 00:52:18,329
for heaven's sake, who are you?

741
00:52:18,637 --> 00:52:20,053
I never saw the like of you

742
00:52:20,809 --> 00:52:25,340
Rasool Allah ﷺ responded, do you think you could keep it secret, if I told you.

743
00:52:25,766 --> 00:52:27,057
So, the man said: Yes.

744
00:52:27,303 --> 00:52:30,926
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I am Muhammad(محمد), the Messenger of Allah.

745
00:52:31,881 --> 00:52:36,316
The shepherd said: You mean you are the one Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) say, claims to be a Sabian(صباء),

746
00:52:36,667 --> 00:52:42,294
Sabian was a degrading accusation that the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) would level towards the Muslims,

747
00:52:42,344 --> 00:52:45,692
they would call them As-Sabioon(ألصابعون), rather than call them Muslim.

748
00:52:45,973 --> 00:52:49,041
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes, they do say that.

749
00:52:49,910 --> 00:52:57,029
The man said: Well, I bear witness that you bring the truth, and that only a prophet could do, as you have

750
00:52:57,361 --> 00:52:59,100
I am your follower now.

751
00:52:59,490 --> 00:53:05,073
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him; You cannot be that right now.

752
00:53:05,369 --> 00:53:09,672
Come and join us, when you hear, I have declared myself openly.

753
00:53:10,372 --> 00:53:13,525
Rasool Ullah doesn't mean that you cannot follow me in terms of becoming Muslim.

754
00:53:13,565 --> 00:53:17,133
It means you cannot join me now, but he did accept his Islam.

755
00:53:17,470 --> 00:53:22,733
But you cannot join the Islamic Jama'ah(جماعة) at the moment and follow Rasool Allah ﷺ

756
00:53:22,773 --> 00:53:25,579
because Rasool Ullah is still at that secretive stage.

757
00:53:26,370 --> 00:53:34,094
So, you can see here the balance between giving Da'wah(دعوة) and protecting the identity of Rasool Allah ﷺ in being secret.

758
00:53:34,397 --> 00:53:40,266
Rasool Allah ﷺ did declare his identity to people whom he thought would be respondent to the Da'wah(دعوة).

759
00:53:40,546 --> 00:53:43,681
But he didn't give Da'wah(دعوة) to every single person he met in Hijrah(هجرة).

760
00:53:44,036 --> 00:53:47,925
Because all of those people Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) would meet and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) would tell them this is a guide.

761
00:53:48,155 --> 00:53:52,493
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not give them Da'wah(دعوة), he did not invite them to Islam.

762
00:53:53,001 --> 00:53:55,139
So, it shows you that there's a balance between the two.

763
00:53:57,102 --> 00:54:00,795
Finally, the Daiyah(داعيه) needs to be financially independent.

764
00:54:01,770 --> 00:54:04,299
When Rasool Allah ﷺ told Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) that

765
00:54:05,003 --> 00:54:06,926
I've been given permission to make Hijrah(هجرة)

766
00:54:07,932 --> 00:54:10,657
and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) told him I will join you and be your companion.

767
00:54:11,370 --> 00:54:17,630
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) told Muhammadﷺ, here are two camels for Hijrah(هجرة).

768
00:54:17,966 --> 00:54:18,997
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

769
00:54:19,091 --> 00:54:19,598
بِثَّمَنْ

770
00:54:19,623 --> 00:54:21,524
I'm going to take the camel and pay for it.

771
00:54:21,894 --> 00:54:24,785
Notice here Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying that he's going to pay for that camel.

772
00:54:25,491 --> 00:54:28,301
So, it's important for the Daiyah(داعيه)to be financially independent.

773
00:54:28,380 --> 00:54:34,384
Because what happens is that, when a scholar is on the government payroll,

774
00:54:34,659 --> 00:54:40,781
there's a conflict of interest when that scholar is giving a fatwa(فتوى) on any issue that relates to the government.

775
00:54:41,349 --> 00:54:43,368
When the government is feeding this scholar,

776
00:54:43,926 --> 00:54:48,974
the scholar will be hesitant to criticize the government.

777
00:54:49,888 --> 00:54:57,411
And there's a clear conflict of interest in any Fatwa(فتوى) that relates to politics or relates to issues that upset the government.

778
00:54:58,105 --> 00:55:06,499
And that's why, for example, we hear issues such as scholars giving Fatwa(فتوى), that it's allowed to have interest banks,

779
00:55:06,757 --> 00:55:10,322
banks that deal with the interest system rather than Islamic banks.

780
00:55:10,801 --> 00:55:16,139
This is for example, a fatwa(فتوى) that was forced upon a scholar or a scholar said it to please the government.

781
00:55:16,874 --> 00:55:18,282
That's just an example.

782
00:55:18,888 --> 00:55:27,108
So, it's important for Dua'aa(دعواء) scholars and preachers who invite to Islam to be financially independent.

783
00:55:28,983 --> 00:55:38,607
Rasool Allah ﷺ, and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) were traveling in the desert, at the peak of the summer season,

784
00:55:39,413 --> 00:55:40,442
it was very hot.

785
00:55:40,679 --> 00:55:42,071
 Ibn Is'haqq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ) says;

786
00:55:42,318 --> 00:55:45,637
Then he took them down, he's referring to the guide

787
00:55:45,848 --> 00:55:52,167
Then he took them down the valley and so to Quba'a(قباء) to the Banni Amr Bin Auf(بني عمرو بن عوف).

788
00:55:52,997 --> 00:55:57,378
It was now Monday the 12th of Rabi Al-Awwal(ربيع اول) and the heat was extreme.

789
00:55:57,651 --> 00:56:00,788
The sun almost having reached its zenith.

790
00:56:01,481 --> 00:56:04,524
So, it was in the middle of summer, very hot

791
00:56:04,963 --> 00:56:08,685
When Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه made Hijrah(هجرة).

792
00:56:09,732 --> 00:56:18,687
The Ansaar(اَنْصار) would go out of Madina every day in the morning in anticipation of meeting Rasool Allah ﷺ and greeting him.

793
00:56:19,500 --> 00:56:22,270
But when the heat becomes too extreme, they would go indoors.

794
00:56:23,042 --> 00:56:28,696
So, one day they went to early in the morning, waiting for Rasool Allah ﷺ, when he didn't show up, they went back in.

795
00:56:29,740 --> 00:56:33,602
There was a Jew who was climbing on, one of their high buildings,

796
00:56:34,091 --> 00:56:37,483
and he saw Muhammadﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) approaching.

797
00:56:38,060 --> 00:56:39,460
They were dressed in white,

798
00:56:40,054 --> 00:56:43,335
the reason why they were dressed in brand new white clothes,

799
00:56:43,508 --> 00:56:46,969
is because Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) met with Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(زبير بن عوام),

800
00:56:47,009 --> 00:56:49,869
who was coming back from a business trip from Syria,

801
00:56:50,113 --> 00:56:54,705
he just brought with him some new clothes, so he gave Rasool Allah and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) gifts

802
00:56:55,184 --> 00:56:58,682
and these are the clothes that they put on when they went into Madina.

803
00:56:58,954 --> 00:57:01,730
So, this Jew saw Muhammadﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) approaching,

804
00:57:02,523 --> 00:57:08,749
so he called with the top of his voice he said: O Arabs here is your man, he arrived.

805
00:57:09,596 --> 00:57:15,164
So, the Ansaar(أنْصَار) rushed towards their weapons and marched out to meet Rasool Allahﷺ.

806
00:57:15,228 --> 00:57:21,806
 You might wonder how come they went dressed in their weapons or putting their weapons on?

807
00:57:22,530 --> 00:57:27,539
The reason could be that this was the tradition that when you meet somebody or you greet him

808
00:57:27,959 --> 00:57:33,433
you go out carrying your weapons and this is still a tradition in some tribal societies

809
00:57:33,458 --> 00:57:39,805
that when they would meet an important guest, they would take their rifles with them to greet that guest.

810
00:57:40,369 --> 00:57:45,670
The other reason could be that the Baiyah(بيعة) that Ansaar gave to Rasool Allah ﷺ was a Baiyah(بيعة) of protection,

811
00:57:46,569 --> 00:57:47,998
they were offering him protection.

812
00:57:48,518 --> 00:57:56,947
So, they were carrying their weapons with them, to show him that here we are ready and prepared to serve you and protect you.

813
00:57:57,956 --> 00:58:02,179
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) arrived and people started greeting them.

814
00:58:02,458 --> 00:58:06,569
Now they arrived at the outskirts of Madina which is Qubaa(قباء)

815
00:58:07,595 --> 00:58:10,710
And Rasool Allah ﷺ stayed there in Qubaa(قباء) for 14 days.

816
00:58:11,480 --> 00:58:16,177
And that is when he built the Masjid(مسجد) of Qubaa(قباء), the first Masjid(مسجد) in Islam.

817
00:58:16,826 --> 00:58:18,096
This Masjid(مسجد) is special,

818
00:58:18,500 --> 00:58:24,036
if you make Wudhuu(وضؤ) at your home and you go to Masjid(مسجد) e Qubaa(قباء) and pray two Rak'a (ركعة),

819
00:58:24,248 --> 00:58:32,485
it counts as if you have made Umrah(عمرة), that is a special virtue to praying in the Masjid(مسجد) of Qubaa(قباء)

820
00:58:33,791 --> 00:58:38,821
Rasool Allah ﷺ stayed in house called, the house of bachelors

821
00:58:38,973 --> 00:58:42,927
because all of the men in there or bachelor, the houseof Sa'ad Bin Khaisamah(سعدبن خيثمه).

822
00:58:43,248 --> 00:58:46,918
Rasool Allah ﷺ stayed there because all of the guests are coming in and out of the house.

823
00:58:47,349 --> 00:58:52,436
So, he didn't want to stay with the family and burden them with, all of these people are coming to meet them.

824
00:58:52,476 --> 00:58:54,810
 So, he stayed in this bachelor's house.

825
00:58:55,561 --> 00:59:02,662
And while he was there, Rasool Allah ﷺ sent messengers to Madina, asking them permission to come in.

826
00:59:03,570 --> 00:59:09,726
So, they sent him a large delegation and they came and met Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

827
00:59:09,750 --> 00:59:12,963
اُدْخُلَا آمِنَيْنِ مُطَاعَيْنْ

828
00:59:13,462 --> 00:59:19,027
 Come in and you are safe and you will be obeyed.

829
00:59:20,008 --> 00:59:23,269
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is not coming to Madina as a guest

830
00:59:23,822 --> 00:59:28,625
he is coming to lead the people of Madina and they came and told him you will be obeyed.

831
00:59:28,675 --> 00:59:29,551
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

832
00:59:29,575 --> 00:59:33,501
وَمَا أَرْسَلْنَا مِنْ رَسُولٍ إِلَّا لِيُطَاعَ بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ ۚ

833
00:59:33,699 --> 00:59:38,259
Every prophet that we have sent or every messenger that we have sent, we sent them to be obeyed.

834
00:59:39,558 --> 00:59:42,283
So, the people should follow the Messengers of Allah.

835
00:59:43,467 --> 00:59:48,359
Now Rasool Allah ﷺ goes into Madina, it was amazing day,

836
00:59:48,963 --> 00:59:50,886
it was a huge celebration,

837
00:59:51,287 --> 00:59:54,539
people came out to greet him, the men came out armed

838
00:59:55,086 --> 00:59:58,377
the Abyssinians were dancing with their spears

839
00:59:59,011 --> 01:00:01,052
women were standing on rooftops,

840
01:00:01,530 --> 01:00:06,423
children were flooding the streets, everybody wants to catch a glimpse of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

841
01:00:07,219 --> 01:00:13,347
Anas Ibn Malik(انس ابن مالك) says; "The messenger of Allah did come and his companion.

842
01:00:14,259 --> 01:00:19,637
They were among the towns people, even the old people came out to greet them,

843
01:00:20,127 --> 01:00:23,647
climbing on top of houses and shouting which one is he?

844
01:00:24,031 --> 01:00:28,064
Anas Ibn Malik(انس ابن مالك) says. "We never saw such a sight before."

845
01:00:28,796 --> 01:00:33,192
People coming out everybody wants to catch a glimpse of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

846
01:00:33,242 --> 01:00:36,280
people were happy that Rasool Allah ﷺ has arrived.

847
01:00:36,597 --> 01:00:42,277
Anas Ibn Malikرضي الله عنه said; "I witnessed the day, he entered among us

848
01:00:42,616 --> 01:00:45,394
and I witnessed the day, he died.

849
01:00:45,957 --> 01:00:48,940
And I never saw two days as those.

850
01:00:49,529 --> 01:00:51,550
I never saw two days like that in my life."

851
01:00:52,205 --> 01:00:54,567
Anas Ibn Malik(انس ابن مالك) says in another narration;

852
01:00:55,693 --> 01:01:00,832
I witness two days, One day was the brightest and best day in my life.

853
01:01:01,084 --> 01:01:04,283
And that was the day Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) came into Madina.

854
01:01:04,747 --> 01:01:08,108
The other day was the darkest day and the worst day in my life.

855
01:01:08,331 --> 01:01:13,792
And that was the day in which Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away and I've witnessed both of them.

856
01:01:14,156 --> 01:01:17,388
So dear brothers and sisters, the best day in Madina has ever witnessed,

857
01:01:17,945 --> 01:01:20,178
was the day in which Rasool Allah ﷺ came in.

858
01:01:20,481 --> 01:01:26,082
And the worst day in Madina has ever witnessed was the day Rasool Allah ﷺ left.

859
01:01:27,983 --> 01:01:33,544
Rasool Allah ﷺ was offered to stay in every house in Madina,

860
01:01:33,835 --> 01:01:35,359
all of them were welcoming.

861
01:01:35,611 --> 01:01:42,554
But Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to stay with Bannu Najjar(بنو نجار), because Bannu Najjar(بنو نجار) are his relatives.

862
01:01:43,736 --> 01:01:48,498
You see, Hashim(هاشم) married a woman from Bannu Najjar(بنو نجار),

863
01:01:48,538 --> 01:01:50,879
Bannu Najjar(بنو نجار) are from Al-Khazraj(ألخزرج).

864
01:01:51,509 --> 01:01:56,734
Therefore, Abdul Muttalib(عبدالمطلب) his maternal uncles are from Madina from Bannu Najjar(بنو نجار).

865
01:01:57,408 --> 01:02:00,386
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I want to stay with Bannu Najjar(بنو نجار).

866
01:02:01,490 --> 01:02:05,874
And then he asked Bannu Najjar(بنو نجار), he said which house of Bannu Najjar(بنو نجار) is closest to me?

867
01:02:06,490 --> 01:02:08,472
So, Abu Ayuub Al-Ansaari(ابوايوب الانصاري) said: My house.

868
01:02:09,107 --> 01:02:11,824
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ stayed at the house of Abu Ayuub(ابوايوب).

869
01:02:12,531 --> 01:02:15,259
Rasool Ullah wanted to stay in the lower level

870
01:02:15,299 --> 01:02:20,093
while Abu Ayuub(ابوايوب) was trying to convince him to stay in the upper level, because it was a two story house.

871
01:02:21,216 --> 01:02:25,582
The reason why, Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to stay in the lower level is because, people are visiting him.

872
01:02:26,490 --> 01:02:31,148
So, he wanted to make it easy and stay in the lower level, finally Abu Ayuub(ابوايوب) agreed

873
01:02:31,891 --> 01:02:38,598
Abu Ayuub(ابوايوب) says; We had a container filled with water that fell.

874
01:02:38,807 --> 01:02:44,737
So, we were afraid that water would drip on Rasool Allah ﷺ,

875
01:02:45,235 --> 01:02:49,284
so we use our blanket, and me and my wife only had that blanket.

876
01:02:49,622 --> 01:02:54,909
We used it, to soak up the water, and we had to sleep without that blanket."

877
01:02:55,527 --> 01:03:01,985
This is the generosity that the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم were offering to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

878
01:03:02,407 --> 01:03:05,476
his only blanket he used it, to soak up water,

879
01:03:05,671 --> 01:03:12,339
just so that a few drops of water wouldn't drip on Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

880
01:03:12,979 --> 01:03:18,033
Another example of the generosity of people in Madina Zaid Bin Thabit رضي الله عنه says;

881
01:03:18,570 --> 01:03:21,080
the first gift made to the Messenger of Allah,

882
01:03:21,451 --> 01:03:26,421
after he took up residence in the home of Abu Ayuub(ابوايوب) was brought to him by myself.

883
01:03:27,076 --> 01:03:29,859
It was a big wooden bowl filled with bread,

884
01:03:30,318 --> 01:03:32,242
crumbled up with milk and butter.

885
01:03:32,798 --> 01:03:35,477
I told him that my mother had sent him the bowl.

886
01:03:35,818 --> 01:03:37,566
He commented, May Allah bless her.

887
01:03:38,159 --> 01:03:40,728
Then he called over his companions and they ate.

888
01:03:41,363 --> 01:03:46,236
Then a wooden bowl came from Sa'ad Ibn Ubadah(سعدابن عبادة), it was bread mixed with meat gravy.

889
01:03:47,533 --> 01:03:49,195
Zaid Bin Thabit(زيد بن ثابت) then says,

890
01:03:49,491 --> 01:03:56,201
not an evening went by, without there being at the door of the Messenger of Allah three or four people

891
01:03:56,468 --> 01:03:59,267
who would come, one after the other carrying food

892
01:04:00,786 --> 01:04:03,989
He remained there in the home of Abu Ayuub(ابوايوب) for seven months.

893
01:04:04,490 --> 01:04:09,126
So, you can just imagine the scene of people coming in everybody carrying a plate, to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

894
01:04:09,159 --> 01:04:14,834
these were poor people but they were giving up their food for Rasool Allah ﷺ.

895
01:04:15,878 --> 01:04:21,298
People loved Rasool Allah ﷺ, young girls went in the streets and they were singing,

896
01:04:22,232 --> 01:04:25,289
they were saying we are girls of Bannu Najjar(بنو نجار).

897
01:04:25,491 --> 01:04:28,243
How wonderful if Muhammad(محمد) were our neighbor.

898
01:04:28,574 --> 01:04:32,783
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: "Allah knows that my heart loves you all.

899
01:04:33,418 --> 01:04:35,530
Allah knows that my heart loves you all."

900
01:04:35,581 --> 01:04:39,362
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ loved them and they loved him.

901
01:04:40,937 --> 01:04:45,986
Allahعَزّوجَلّ has chosen the people of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار) to be the Ansaar(أنْصَار) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

902
01:04:46,425 --> 01:04:50,556
They loved him very much and he also loved them a lot.

903
01:04:50,837 --> 01:04:56,709
Towards the end of his life, he said, If it wasn't for Hijrah(هجرة), I would consider myself to be a member of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار).

904
01:04:58,671 --> 01:05:00,849
What was the situation of Madina like?

905
01:05:01,511 --> 01:05:06,345
When Rasool Allah ﷺ moved in there, there were five tribes living in Madina.

906
01:05:07,176 --> 01:05:09,392
Three of them were Jewish, and two of them were Arab.

907
01:05:10,359 --> 01:05:15,174
The three Jewish tribes were Bannu Qainuqah(بنو قينقاع), Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير), Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه).

908
01:05:15,906 --> 01:05:19,588
Bannu Qainuqah(بنو قينقاع) lived in the center of Madina, the market place

909
01:05:20,144 --> 01:05:22,771
and they were in the business of jewelry.

910
01:05:24,109 --> 01:05:30,799
They used to live in the outskirts of Madina in forts, but they were driven out in a war between them and other Jews.

911
01:05:31,511 --> 01:05:35,213
So, they ended up settling in the middle of Madina, in the center of the town.

912
01:05:36,765 --> 01:05:41,385
Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير), and Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه) lived in the outskirts of Madina.

913
01:05:42,152 --> 01:05:48,686
And they were living in forts they had about 59 fortresses in which they lived in.

914
01:05:49,363 --> 01:05:52,232
Their fighting force was about 2000.

915
01:05:52,578 --> 01:05:56,360
These were the men of fighting age, about 2000.

916
01:05:57,312 --> 01:06:00,417
The Arab tribes were Al-Aos(الاوس) and Al-Khazraj(الخزرج)

917
01:06:01,759 --> 01:06:04,847
and they're fighting force was about 4000.

918
01:06:05,164 --> 01:06:10,590
 And they lived inside Madina, one tribe lived in north and the other tribe lived in the south.

919
01:06:10,648 --> 01:06:16,200
So, Madina wasn't really a city in terms of all houses being connected,

920
01:06:16,500 --> 01:06:23,594
but it was a collection of small villages that formed Madina.

921
01:06:24,200 --> 01:06:27,868
So, you'd have living quarters for the Jews and living quarters for the Arabs

922
01:06:27,918 --> 01:06:33,690
and each Jewish tribe was separate and two Arab tribes are also separate.

923
01:06:34,597 --> 01:06:39,233
The livelihoods of the people in Madina was based on agriculture.

924
01:06:39,666 --> 01:06:42,716
It was fertile, and they had palm groves

925
01:06:43,660 --> 01:06:48,381
The farmer would need money throughout the year, until harvest time would come,

926
01:06:48,684 --> 01:06:56,077
So the Jewish tribes would lend the Arabs money and they would charge them interest, for usury,

927
01:06:56,315 --> 01:07:03,360
 and this cause some conflict and some bitter feelings between the Arabs and the Jews of Madina.

928
01:07:03,582 --> 01:07:09,021
This is briefly the situation that existed prior to the advent of Islam.

929
01:07:09,500 --> 01:07:17,889
Now when the slam came in, now we have Muslims, you have pagan worshippers and you have Jews.

930
01:07:18,465 --> 01:07:23,196
So, you had different faiths and different ethnic groups inside Madina.

931
01:07:23,936 --> 01:07:30,081
And Rasool Allah ﷺ had to be very careful in dealing with these complications in Madina,

932
01:07:30,106 --> 01:07:36,010
don't think that it was very easy and everybody just became Muslim and everybody loved Rasool Allah ﷺ

933
01:07:36,249 --> 01:07:40,145
and it was very easy to rule over Madina, it was very difficult.

934
01:07:40,760 --> 01:07:44,721
You had people among the Arabs, who were not happy, that Rasool Allah ﷺ was there,

935
01:07:45,082 --> 01:07:49,682
you also had the Jewish tribes who were not happy that Rasool Allah ﷺ was there,

936
01:07:50,141 --> 01:07:52,895
and then among the Arabs, we had Muslim and non Muslim.

937
01:07:53,097 --> 01:07:57,002
So, it was a complicated situation, to give you an example of this complication.

938
01:07:57,216 --> 01:08:03,525
Rasool Allah ﷺ was riding on his donkey and he went towards a gathering

939
01:08:04,275 --> 01:08:08,823
that included Arabs, Muslim and non Muslim and also Jews.

940
01:08:09,608 --> 01:08:15,086
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ went to that gathering and when his donkey arrived,

941
01:08:15,526 --> 01:08:20,898
obviously it caused some dust and Abdullah Bin Ubaey(عبدالله بن اُبَيْ),

942
01:08:21,297 --> 01:08:24,007
who later became the head of the Munafiqeen(منافقين),

943
01:08:24,151 --> 01:08:25,890
he said, keep your dust away from us.

944
01:08:26,680 --> 01:08:31,358
And Rasool Ullah did not respond back to him, Rasool Ullah started preaching Islam to them.

945
01:08:32,305 --> 01:08:34,659
He gave them a talk about Islam

946
01:08:34,844 --> 01:08:36,749
When he finished Abdullah Bin Ubaey(عبدالله بن اُبَيْ) said,

947
01:08:37,188 --> 01:08:42,764
Don't come and bother us in our meetings with your talk, stay home,

948
01:08:43,223 --> 01:08:47,061
and whoever comes to visit you, then tell them your stories.

949
01:08:48,067 --> 01:08:50,640
Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحه), who was a Muslim

950
01:08:50,680 --> 01:08:54,971
 He said; No, we want him to come to our meetings and talk to us.

951
01:08:55,586 --> 01:08:59,814
And then people started shouting and war was almost going to break out.

952
01:09:00,274 --> 01:09:02,738
And Rasool Allah ﷺ had to calm them down,

953
01:09:03,063 --> 01:09:06,872
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ went to the house of Sa'ad Ibn Ubadah(سعدبن عبادة) and said;

954
01:09:07,129 --> 01:09:09,561
O Sa'ad(سعد) didn't you see, what Abdullah Bin Ubaey(عبدالله بن اُبَيْ) did?

955
01:09:10,918 --> 01:09:13,643
Sa'ad asked him, what happened and when Rasool Allah ﷺ told him.

956
01:09:13,946 --> 01:09:15,705
Sa'ad(سعد) responded back by saying;

957
01:09:15,909 --> 01:09:19,995
O Rasool Allah, Abdullah Bin Ubaey(عبدالله بن اُبَيْ) was a man,

958
01:09:20,303 --> 01:09:24,493
whom his people were almost going to appoint him, King over them.

959
01:09:25,167 --> 01:09:29,961
When you arrived, so he sees that you have stripped him of his kingdom,

960
01:09:30,295 --> 01:09:31,759
you have stripped him of that post.

961
01:09:31,839 --> 01:09:37,193
So, Sa'ad Ibn Ubadah(سعدبن عبادة) is telling, Rasool Allah ﷺ it's understandable that he is against you,

962
01:09:37,501 --> 01:09:41,788
because he was going to be appointed by Al-Khazraj(الخزرج) to be king over them.

963
01:09:43,535 --> 01:09:48,741
So, this was the situation that Rasool Allah ﷺ was dealing with.

964
01:09:49,131 --> 01:09:54,347
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

965
01:09:54,629 --> 01:09:57,305
وَالسلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

